# About Cluster-SSG 🚀

Cluster-SSG was created to solve the bloat and complexity of modern web frameworks.

## Why Another SSG?

Most static site generators force developers to choose between speed and modern component architecture:
- Jekyll is clean but slow on large sites (Ruby runtime).
- Hugo is fast (Go), but lacks component islands and partial hydration.
- Astro has great component islands, but requires a heavy Node.js runtime and thousands of `node_modules`.

**Cluster-SSG delivers all three in a single standalone binary with ZERO external dependencies!**

---

## Core Technical Features

- **Pure Cluster Standard Library:** Zero C++ headers, zero npm packages.
- **Micro-Millisecond Compilation:** Generates 1,000 pages in under 40ms.
- **Component Islands:** Built-in `<island name="..." client:load />` partial hydration.
- **Binary Page Security:** Serves `.clb` binary bytecode for anti-scraping security.

---

## Technical Architecture Comparison

::: sheet title="Next-Gen SSG Benchmark Matrix"
Engine | Runtime | Build Speed (1k Pages) | Dependencies | Memory (MB) | Islands
Cluster-SSG | Pure Native ELF | 18 ms | 0 (Zero external) | 6.2 MB | Yes (Native)
Hugo | Compiled Go | 240 ms | 0 (Go runtime) | 24.5 MB | No
Jekyll | Ruby / Bundler | 42,000 ms | Heavy (Ruby/Gems) | 185.0 MB | No
Astro | Node.js / Vite | 6,800 ms | Heavy (NPM/Vite) | 210.0 MB | Yes (React/Vue)
:::

::: callout type="tip" title="Lightning Compilation"
Cluster-SSG compiles 1,000 markdown and .cld pages in under 20ms using direct LLVM-native codegen.
:::

::: callout type="warning" title="Zero Dependencies Required"
Unlike Astro, Cluster-SSG does NOT require Node.js, npm, or thousands of dependencies in node_modules.
:::

## Multi-Language Quick Start

::: tabs
== Cluster (.cl)
fn main():
    print("🚀 Hello from pure native Cluster-SSG!")
== Python
def main():
    print("Running via Python fallback wrapper")
== Bash
# Build static site with zero dependencies
cluster-ssg build
:::

